        "original_id": "75bfcbbf-c66d-5e9a-b351-cfce213bc8a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Hawks, Arthur Berthelet, Katharine Hepburn, Cary Grant\n- Films: Bringing Up Baby\n- Companies: RKO Radio Pictures\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: classic Hollywood era, silent movies, stage plays, Broadway, screwball comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Berthelet was an American film director who lived from 1879 to 1949.\n- Arthur Berthelet moved from directing stage plays, including several on Broadway, to directing silent movies.\n- Howard Hawks was born on May 30, 1896, and died on December 26, 1977.\n- Howard Hawks was an American film director, producer, and screenwriter of the classic Hollywood era.\n- Bringing Up Baby is a 1938 American screwball comedy film.\n- Bringing Up Baby was directed by Howard Hawks.\n- Bringing Up Baby starred Katharine Hepburn and Cary Grant.\n- RKO Radio Pictures released Bringing Up Baby.",
